      "pins": ["J11.1", "J11.2", "U2.13", "U4.1", "U4.2", "D1.2", "R2.1"],
      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/NET0011", "GND"],
      "observed": "A screw terminal J11 is connected between the heater-control net and ground: J11 pin 2 is on /Microcontroller/NET0011, which also contains ESP32 GPIO1, TPS1H200 IN/DIAG_EN, and the status LED; J11 pin 1 is on GND.",
      "expected": "The specification describes GPIO1 as the sole heater-control driver to the high-side switch IN/DIAG_EN and the onboard status LED; it does not describe an external screw terminal that can pull that control net to ground. Standard practice would not place a user-accessible short path directly across an MCU output and GND without current limiting or a defined input interface.",
      "evidence": [
