        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"8\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J11\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net /Microcontroller/HEATER)"}
      ],
      "impact": "If J11 is jumpered or wired closed, GPIO1 and the TPS1H200 IN/DIAG_EN net are shorted to GND, preventing heater turn-on and potentially overloading the ESP32 GPIO when firmware attempts to drive it high.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist otherwise matches the specified power, thermocouple, fan, USB, and heater-switch architecture, but it contains an unmentioned screw terminal J11 that can short the GPIO1 heater-control net to ground."
}

